<title>JAPAN: Tokyo stock market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo stock market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo stock market is closed on Monday for a national holiday. It will reopen on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, the key 225-issue Nikkei average closed down 210.61 points or 0.99 percent at 21,112.24. Its key December futures shed 140 points to end at 21,180.</p>
